class Solution {
  public int[] parcelBudgetProofStrip(int[][] drawers, int k) {
    int[][] a=drawers; List<Integer> out=new ArrayList<>();
    {int[]dp=new int[k+1];for(int[]item:a)for(int c=k;c>=item[0];c--)dp[c]=Math.max(dp[c],dp[c-item[0]]+item[1]);for(int x:dp)out.add(x);}
    return out.stream().mapToInt(Integer::intValue).toArray();
  }
}

privateData.editorialMd:
The working idea

Each parcel is [weight,value], with positive weight and nonnegative value. For every capacity from 0 through k, produce the maximum total value obtainable by choosing each parcel at most once and using no more than that capacity.

Return the entire derived sequence, preserving its order.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(n*k); space O(k).

